1803.6 Geotechnical reports. A geotechnical engineering report shall be prepared for all sites and submitted to the
commissioner.
Exception: One- and two-family dwellings no more than three stories in height shall not require a geotechnical
report except where any of the following exist:
1. Shallow foundations are used that bear on or above compressible soils (see Section 1803.4.4), uncontrolled
fill (see Section 1806.2.3), or artificially treated soils (see Section 1806.2.4);
2. Underpinning is required;
3. The structure is within the special flood hazard area;
4. Dewatering is required;
5. Test pits are implemented in lieu of borings as per Section 1803.4.1; or
6. As required by the commissioner.
